#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179593 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179731 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e281dd-40c0-515a-a5d5-d063609ecf73" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to X"}] :question/id #uuid "30d54dcc-49a2-5cd0-9eb9-659413ed5c67" :question/math-academy-id "e-9525" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x,$ where $C=C_1 \\cup C_2$ is the path comprising of two line segments, as shown below.\n\n![](images/3d/3d408de0d50e2688aa0b35d8af39b6847cfdf21d5ec583320f0204384304fbc8.png)" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x = x_2 - x_1,\n$$\n\nwhere $x_2$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and $x_1$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, $x_2 = -3$ and $x_1 = 3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d x = x_2 - x_1 = (-3) - 3 = -6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179594 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179732 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6935944-0acd-5593-aa80-e56f6014c13f" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to Y"}] :question/id #uuid "d799bcde-dbf0-580e-921b-18e56d729ea1" :question/math-academy-id "e-9526" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y,$ where $C$ is the path along the semicircle of radius $3,$ traversed from the point $(3,0)$ to the point $(-3,0),$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/ca/ca97546ecaf9e37bee53fcc2b0c66962cff67a91ee9b117cc8ac8531efa23efc.png)" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y = y_2 - y_1,\n$$\n\nwhere $y_2$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and $y_1$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, $y_2 = 0$ and $y_1 = 0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d y = y_2 - y_1 =  0 - 0 = 0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179595 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179733 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/id #uuid "e1d24f1c-4b7c-5c5e-bf93-7f9e76dffdf2" :question/math-academy-id "e-9527" :question/problem "If $\\displaystyle\\int_{C} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x= 8$ and $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x= -2,$ calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x$ given that $C = C_1\\cup C_2.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C = C_1\\cup C_2$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x = -\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x$\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x = \\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x + \\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =-(-2)-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 8 & =2-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_2} f(x,y) \\,\\textrm d x = -6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179996 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179732 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6935944-0acd-5593-aa80-e56f6014c13f" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ba37e23-4407-593f-878c-8abbf9aaeab1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415630} {:answer/id #uuid "2cfb5012-01ba-5773-8380-07b0c227978b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415631} {:answer/id #uuid "5350f40c-1597-5be9-bd8f-3c625b18eb6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415637} {:answer/id #uuid "627a50c9-9a65-5ce4-b1c6-1df26867b7d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415640} {:answer/id #uuid "a8ef58cc-01f9-5539-9409-f4b9eb5a98f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "627a50c9-9a65-5ce4-b1c6-1df26867b7d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415640} :answer-field/id #uuid "11d73d0a-9b92-5725-b122-3966ab941aac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415670}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "64880fd8-5a53-573e-8070-ad8f3985f4a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-124126" :question/problem "![](images/ec/ec03c28e17138917d31898f165925cb246cf1f81a03f15672f87dde586b06ed2.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is the path comprising of a horizontal line segment of length $2$ and a semicircle of radius $2,$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{2}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{1}={y}_{2}=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1}=1-1=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180001 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179732 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6935944-0acd-5593-aa80-e56f6014c13f" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2384c997-1d5d-53b4-a312-5c2ec9c86073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257079} {:answer/id #uuid "6458baf9-7035-53af-916d-1b7d57ec3bfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257663} {:answer/id #uuid "c6df00e4-14bf-5e23-a939-f984f68a0ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258519} {:answer/id #uuid "e3cc3553-89e2-5ace-abc4-1172afe072cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258761} {:answer/id #uuid "e497e2c8-05df-595e-a19c-1ff2ed39c04b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2384c997-1d5d-53b4-a312-5c2ec9c86073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257079} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4304b44-cbb1-57e3-b024-663ea2e2eb70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46935a1e-c060-58a7-ab7d-a527906c3000" :question/math-academy-id "q-124148" :question/problem "![](images/24/2400f92070b4f7d4e0ad0309574b729da86754bc64b6d7a3c508433d1bbc7f76.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment between the points $(4,0)$ to the point $(0,3),$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{2}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{2}=3$ and ${y}_{1}=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1}=3-0=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179733 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d06d74e-8cbb-534e-9e3d-b565ad2be03c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257326} {:answer/id #uuid "3e4cf246-885b-5339-ba6d-2a6a26c29fd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Impossible to determine" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257341} {:answer/id #uuid "9c24bf18-5b81-5f28-9b53-d40d50783a35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258154} {:answer/id #uuid "a96067c9-1bd3-5cae-ad8c-0d00c40ff765" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258259} {:answer/id #uuid "c8e8aab0-bd61-54e0-9a37-1cee850b0d7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a96067c9-1bd3-5cae-ad8c-0d00c40ff765" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258259} :answer-field/id #uuid "564a707d-5cc2-58d4-811e-f0cb1791bf4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4dcfed6a-aece-5954-8f2d-d015ef026f97" :question/math-academy-id "q-124149" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=4$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=6,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4-6 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180003 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179733 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f5989ee-33da-5aee-80b5-59f4458347c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415633} {:answer/id #uuid "608438d6-dac5-5e73-81f2-28ee2e83a8a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415639} {:answer/id #uuid "65d7c98e-321b-597f-b317-1c771751881a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415641} {:answer/id #uuid "ba35a350-5197-53ed-ab93-7811ac616cc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415657} {:answer/id #uuid "f61c2696-a894-5f2d-b3e9-6c094b9ebfe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba35a350-5197-53ed-ab93-7811ac616cc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415657} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ae3b474-71b1-5e53-80d8-8ff83014500b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e3ca1583-0f44-5bd8-a174-1f7bba09e7fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-124150" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=12$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=8,$ calculate ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 12 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 12 & =-8-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 20 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-20.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415678 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179733 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75d3c873-74de-59e1-9205-f943f90ed6f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415644} {:answer/id #uuid "7e5524bb-b193-5580-b930-13a4c434d2d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415647} {:answer/id #uuid "87d96269-00c7-5980-b0c5-a6b5955bd666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415648} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ba360f-ed62-5d53-a965-3d462320b72e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Impossible to determine" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415655} {:answer/id #uuid "d44d1f9d-b5f4-53e0-ba1f-2259d7fb76a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e5524bb-b193-5580-b930-13a4c434d2d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415647} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bc8f0e0-f5cb-5cee-aa30-efe616caf6e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415675}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "41a5f2bb-63fd-5596-b20f-47e35c05d2ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-124183" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=14$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-6,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =14-(-6) \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259614 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179733 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28d5e447-8418-5713-9439-d989ec5b6429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257147} {:answer/id #uuid "361a934d-451b-5e92-92f4-46a6a1e2211a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257259} {:answer/id #uuid "dc5e7fd0-81d0-5309-8978-db5e8c201730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258701} {:answer/id #uuid "e9498204-facb-59b8-b6f0-bc76230762a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258805} {:answer/id #uuid "f3c4005f-481d-5307-83cd-ce0861f8586f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9498204-facb-59b8-b6f0-bc76230762a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258805} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5a217e9-fa91-5a9c-b987-36a79f55e03e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7673d1a0-afd2-5d22-93cd-75c43bd54a25" :question/math-academy-id "q-124186" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=16$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=11,$ calculate ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -{\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -16 & =-11+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -5 & ={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415677 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179733 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fd19952-77af-5f27-a7ef-adf46b1958ae" :knowledge-point/title "Orientation-Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01e4d0b1-3d49-5ae5-b65b-8dbe801177f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415622} {:answer/id #uuid "2a14506d-1bc5-538f-8601-a75415c5af4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415629} {:answer/id #uuid "328548aa-6ec4-5ded-abca-468351c78e63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415634} {:answer/id #uuid "53d99d5e-8f7a-5890-a03d-e22ee095b634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415638} {:answer/id #uuid "7b192eed-e4b2-5e18-b229-5a2f13c347d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01e4d0b1-3d49-5ae5-b65b-8dbe801177f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415622} :answer-field/id #uuid "45a9fe64-c73b-5f9f-af73-48b5821ab772" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "28b25a72-e404-5d69-993b-a9b2c8d9ba39" :question/math-academy-id "q-124187" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=17,$ ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=7,$ and ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=5,$ calculate ${\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 17 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+5-{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 17 & =-7+5-{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ 19 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-19.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415679 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179731 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e281dd-40c0-515a-a5d5-d063609ecf73" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to X"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18b46eaa-8958-53b6-8687-3a9f1e7e95dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415626} {:answer/id #uuid "69547d52-da29-51bf-acae-befe4ab3ec6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415642} {:answer/id #uuid "8f3d2128-0a37-5623-9bd3-50d58517585b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415650} {:answer/id #uuid "928dd7bb-83bc-5472-82e3-9788fdbdebd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415651} {:answer/id #uuid "d91dbfa3-7b7e-59a5-96a6-b