he point $(0,2)$ to the point $(1,1),$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${x}_{2}=1$ and ${x}_{1}=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1}=1-0=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415676 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179731 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e281dd-40c0-515a-a5d5-d063609ecf73" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to X"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05561efb-810b-5987-b7e5-1cc8fd5d9c6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415623} {:answer/id #uuid "29b4934d-6ad2-57c3-89d5-064138568fd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415628} {:answer/id #uuid "3dec085f-d086-5935-8b12-c7f060d85182" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415636} {:answer/id #uuid "8d3c001b-a296-5526-af04-84e4bd0dfc8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415649} {:answer/id #uuid "d43c3421-a359-5d67-9fb2-039db4f6dbbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29b4934d-6ad2-57c3-89d5-064138568fd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415628} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a420733-9597-59c7-a430-a56589724b06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "19c93f12-207e-5d48-9d03-3dc16bfb7738" :question/math-academy-id "q-124313" :question/problem "![](images/fb/fbc6ddf87d5f5502db656242222dca27fb33ded5d3bdcf372b70ef10eda07624.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the path along a three-quarter circle of radius $3,$ traversed from the point $(-1,-3)$ to the point $(-4,0),$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${x}_{2}=-4$ and ${x}_{1}=-1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1}=(-4)-(-1)=-3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415682 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179731 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e281dd-40c0-515a-a5d5-d063609ecf73" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to X"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17e8204a-f6c5-582c-9a70-1391bf4c46e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415625} {:answer/id #uuid "21124427-bf82-58d2-a56e-34687e5df13f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415627} {:answer/id #uuid "3686abdb-2eb3-5b8d-95fd-3506ce16b7bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415635} {:answer/id #uuid "b96c24b7-dfe8-55e1-bbe2-db59a4ed77de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415656} {:answer/id #uuid "fb0dd7b5-2212-5d4a-9021-9a9a33ba834c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415666}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb0dd7b5-2212-5d4a-9021-9a9a33ba834c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415666} :answer-field/id #uuid "77c94cbf-f9ef-59ad-9086-7c8d91862986" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "caee1f70-9af3-5daf-82bf-4723f96ead82" :question/math-academy-id "q-124329" :question/problem "![](images/77/77c069c4b4306b3337a44ddfc53ecd4d727e78da09d77d61e84fc01d3b30c302.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C$ is the closed path along the square of \nside $2,$ traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, the initial and terminal points are the same (since the path is closed and is traversed only once). Therefore, ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$ and we have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259675 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179732 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6935944-0acd-5593-aa80-e56f6014c13f" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2edaaf2f-2729-5e65-a17a-4523df70dc44" :answer