y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{1}=4$ and  ${y}_{2}=-1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1}=(-1)-4=-5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259679 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179732 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6935944-0acd-5593-aa80-e56f6014c13f" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06ca0885-40bb-54cb-993c-16ff6bf31c41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256840} {:answer/id #uuid "12fa8929-0c5a-5ace-90d7-c5115bf0058b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256953} {:answer/id #uuid "183c8bbd-3c11-5936-9ffc-c6982100aaf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256992} {:answer/id #uuid "500abeff-f88a-5e7f-b4d5-355a04de8c57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257467} {:answer/id #uuid "efca4aee-a601-54e9-a99b-317ab7d1d962" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "183c8bbd-3c11-5936-9ffc-c6982100aaf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256992} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ac8b6b8-ab1c-5e1c-a116-351ff4b5cdb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259077}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "239dd34c-3202-5609-97c3-2d198c5bc0b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-124348" :question/problem "![](images/9b/9b3065e58decfca5355252b93ec3283cc5ffc96dc04826aeab1131e95d3a2e64.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the closed path along the rectangle, traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{2}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, the initial and terminal points are the same (since the path is closed and is traversed only once). Therefore, ${y}_{1}={y}_{2},$ and we have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259680 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179732 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6935944-0acd-5593-aa80-e56f6014c13f" :knowledge-point/title "Line Integrals of Unity With Respect to Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1158d026-709a-5659-b93a-fc893dd400af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256940} {:answer/id #uuid "66f2a44e-1a4e-533c-a949-20a791d8a9db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257693} {:answer/id #uuid "9b7e9c21-404c-5ea0-9e7f-5577a4f7ed1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258149} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f700a2-042f-52d1-89e7-50faf272ccdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258207} {:answer/id #uuid "ab1542bb-657e-5259-b224-f4b76e1d04c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab1542bb-657e-5259-b224-f4b76e1d04c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258274} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a1a50c1-b1c0-541a-8298-c9ff23e9c190" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259304}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "76093563-4073-5ddf-89ae-28178104bcaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-124349" :question/problem "![](images/0d/0da125535534cbd50b96cb280cf8b8a4b58653a344c8699d7b732ec73cc3b2ce.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the closed path along a right triangle, traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{2}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, the initial and terminal points are the same (since the path is closed and is traversed only once). Therefore, ${y}_{1}={y}_{2},$ and we have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$"}]}
